Chapter: ImgLongname

  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 The guest reading an image the HOST wrote, which is the only arm that can tell
 the two VFAT implementations apart. build-img.ps1 writes long-name runs in
 PowerShell; Fat16.codex reads them in Codex. A round trip through either one
 alone would pass while proving nothing about the other, which is the shape
 BrotliBeatsOpus was written about.

 The fixture is six chapters chosen for the name shapes that discriminate, not
 for realism:

   X86_64CodeGen.codex   19 characters, two records. The name the old flat SRC/
                         layout mangled to X86_64CO.COD, which is why on-disk
                         cite resolution could never find it.
   readme.codex          differs from its own 8.3 form only in CASE, so it
                         still needs a run; a writer that compared case-blindly
                         would store README.COD and this arm would catch it.
   Thirtee.codex         thirteen characters: exactly one record, no terminator.
   Fourteen.codex        fourteen: exactly two, and the second holds one unit.
   CollideOne.codex      these two share their first six characters, so their
   CollideTwo.codex      aliases must differ by the number after the tilde.

 Any name ending in `.codex` needs a run whatever its base, because the format
 stores three extension characters and `codex` is five. That is the whole
 reason this work existed, and it is why no arm here can test the no-run path
 through a `.codex` fixture -- `codex/test/fat16-longname` covers that on names
 the guest writes itself.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    vol <- fat16-init 2048
    print-line-uni ("usable " & show (fat16-vol-is-usable vol))

    entries <- fat16-list-dir vol "SRC"
    print-line-uni ("SRC entries " & show (list-length entries))

    chapters <- list-files "SRC" ".codex"
    print-line-uni ("list-files SRC .codex " & show (list-length chapters))
    print-line-uni ("names " & img-texts chapters 0 (list-length chapters) "")

    a <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/X86_64CodeGen.codex"
    print-line-uni ("X86_64CodeGen.codex " & img-head a)

    ghost <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/X86_64CO.COD"
    print-line-uni ("no truncated ghost " & img-head ghost)

    b <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/readme.codex"
    print-line-uni ("readme.codex " & img-head b)

    c <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/Thirtee.codex"
    print-line-uni ("Thirtee.codex " & img-head c)

    d <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/Fourteen.codex"
    print-line-uni ("Fourteen.codex " & img-head d)

    e <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/CollideOne.codex"
    print-line-uni ("CollideOne.codex " & img-head e)

    f <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/CollideTwo.codex"
    print-line-uni ("CollideTwo.codex " & img-head f)

    absent <- fat16-read-source vol "SRC/NotThere.codex"
    print-line-uni ("absent " & img-head absent)
  end

Section: Reporting

 The first line rather than the whole chapter, so a wrong cluster chain shows
 as wrong TEXT rather than as a length that happens to match.

  img-head : Maybe Text -> Text
  img-head (m) = when m
    is Just (t) -> img-first-line t 0 (text-length t) ""
    is None -> "<none>"

  img-first-line : Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  img-first-line (t) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if char-code (char-at t i) == from-unicode 10 then acc
    else img-first-line t (i + 1) n (acc & char-encode (char-at t i))

  img-texts : List Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  img-texts (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let piece = list-at xs i & " "
    in img-texts xs (i + 1) n (acc & piece)

